# LeaseTracker AI Cursor Rules

Follow spec.md and AGENTS.md.

Keep Version 1 simple.

Do not add features that are not required by spec.md.

Use clear, beginner-friendly code.

Prefer small reusable functions.

Do not add unnecessary dependencies.

Do not add a database unless explicitly requested.

Do not add authentication.

Do not add payment processing.

Do not add accounting or tax filing functionality.

Use deterministic application logic for all financial calculations.

Never use AI to calculate rent, VAT, CWT, CUSA,
expected cash, outstanding balances, or YTD totals.

Do not hardcode VAT, CWT, CUSA VAT, or escalation rates.
Always use the values stored in the lease data.

Handle rent-free periods correctly.

Use anonymized sample data only.

Never include API keys, passwords, credentials,
confidential information, or real tenant information.

Keep the AI feature small and separate from financial calculations.

Use a free local or open-source approach for the AI feature.
Do not require a paid OpenAI or Claude API.

Write automated tests for important calculation logic.

Before making a major change, check that it is required by spec.md.

If there are multiple possible solutions, choose the simplest solution that satisfies the assignment.
